# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore
#
# The build context for BOTH images is this repository root (npm workspaces
# monorepo - a single package-lock.json lives here), so patterns must cover
# nested paths. Docker matches these against the full relative path, which
# means a bare `.env` only ever matches the top-level file; `**/.env` is what
# actually excludes client/.env and server/.env.
#
# Two jobs: keep the build context small, and never bake local secrets into an
# image layer, where they survive forever even if a later layer "removes" them.
#
# CAUTION: do not ignore server/docker-entrypoint.sh. server/Dockerfile COPYs it
# and excluding it fails the build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image) --------------------------
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log*

# ---- Build output (rebuilt inside the image) ------------------------------
**/dist
**/build
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Secrets: never enter the image ---------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example

# ---- Runtime data: recreated as a mounted volume ---------------------------
**/uploads
**/coverage
**/.vitest

# ---- Tests and tooling ------------------------------------------------------
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/eslint.config.js

# ---- Local scripts and logs -------------------------------------------------
scripts/
**/*.log
**/*.err

# ---- VCS and editor --------------------------------------------------------
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
